    "To the extent permitted by law, the Service is provided “as is” and “as available.” We do not control the accuracy, legality, quality, or conduct associated with User Content or event participants. Organizers and uploaders remain responsible for their decisions, content, permissions, and independent backups.": "i det omfang loven tillader det, leveres Tjenesten \"som den er\" og \"som tilgængelig\". vi kontrollerer ikke nøjagtigheden, lovligheden, kvaliteten eller adfærden i forbindelse med brugerindhold eller eventdeltagere. arrangører og uploadere er fortsat ansvarlige for deres beslutninger, indhold, tilladelser og uafhængige sikkerhedskopier.",
    "Nothing in these terms excludes rights or liability that cannot lawfully be excluded. Subject to that rule, any liability cap, excluded loss categories, and country-specific consumer rights must be completed before launch: [LIABILITY TERMS — TO BE COMPLETED].": "intet i disse vilkår udelukker rettigheder eller ansvar, som ikke lovligt kan udelukkes. denne regel skal ethvert ansvarsloft, udelukkede tabskategorier og landespecifikke forbrugerrettigheder udfyldes inden lanceringen: [LIABILITY TERMS — TO BE COMPLETED].",
    "These terms are governed by [GOVERNING LAW — TO BE COMPLETED]. Courts or dispute-resolution bodies located in [VENUE — TO BE COMPLETED] will have jurisdiction, except where mandatory consumer law gives you the right to bring a claim elsewhere. Before starting formal proceedings, you and SnapUp Events should try in good faith to resolve the issue through the contact details below.": "disse vilkår er reguleret af [GOVERNING LAW — TO BE COMPLETED]. ret eller tvistbilæggelsesorganer i [VENUE — TO BE COMPLETED] vil have kompetence, medmindre den obligatoriske forbrugerlovgivning giver dig ret til at fremsætte et krav andetsteds. inden du starter formelle procedurer, bør du og SnapUp Events i god tro forsøge at løse problemet gennem kontaktoplysningerne nedenfor.",
